[agent] ## Summary
[agent] **Offline feature table — done, on the platform.** All compute ran platform-side in BigQuery (the feature store's BigQuery backing dataset `mlpab_mlpabab879a`):
[agent] 1. `bq load` → raw table `feature_history_raw` (574 rows).
[agent] 2. A single SQL job computed the point-in-time-correct features (`ROW_NUMBER() ... ORDER BY event_time DESC` filtered to `event_time <= T` where **T = 1773478800000**), applied `score = ROUND(sigmoid(-0.4331·f1 - 0.4499·f2 + 1.9204·f3 - 0.0086), 6)`, and wrote the result to the feature table **`scores36e30a`**.
[agent] Result verified:
[agent] - **80 rows, one per account**, columns exactly `account_id, score`, record key `account_id`.
[agent] - Point-in-time logic confirmed on `A0000`: latest revision at/before T is `event_time=1772305740000`, and the later revision `1773979380000` (> T) is correctly excluded → `score = 0.812992`.
[agent] **Online / low-latency serving — cannot be done through the permitted interface (missing capability).**
[agent] The task requires registering the table for online real-time lookup where the platform distinguishes online vs offline. On Vertex AI this is a **Feature Online Store + Feature View** (and optionally a Feature Group over the BQ table). Those live under `gcloud ai feature-online-stores`, `gcloud ai feature-views`, and `gcloud ai feature-groups`.
[agent] - The permitted GA `gcloud ai` surface (this build, 573.0.0) exposes only: `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs`. All feature-store groups return `Invalid choice` — there is **no feature-group / feature-online-store / feature-view / featurestore command**.
[agent] - The Vertex AI Feature Store commands are only under `gcloud alpha/beta ai`, which the harness hard-blocks (`DENIED: gcloud beta is off-interface`).
[agent] - `bq` can create the BigQuery-backed offline table (done) but has no way to provision an online store or feature view.
[agent] So the offline deliverable exists on the platform with the exact name, schema, key, and correct scores; the **online-serving registration is not achievable via the interface under test** because the allowed `gcloud ai` GA CLI has no Feature Store / Feature Online Store command group and the beta/alpha surface where it lives is blocked. No Vertex resources were created (so no `${MLPAB_GCP_PREFIX}_` prefixing was needed), and no extra datasets were created.
